---
// Lore section: the three-stage timeline fully expanded with quest and event details.
// All content is in the initial HTML.
const stages = [
  {
    era: "500 years ago",
    title: "The Dragon of Dragonspine",
    body: [
      "The original Durin was a shadow dragon created by Rhinedottir, the alchemist known as Gold, in Khaenri'ah before the Cataclysm — holding the title of Humus, second only to Albedo the Chalk among her creations.",
      "Gentle at heart, he caused destruction without meaning to. During the Cataclysm he flew to Mondstadt wanting to befriend its people and Dvalin, yet his presence brought ruin alongside the Abyss creatures.",
      "Barbatos and Dvalin fought him down, and his body crashed into Dragonspine. His toxic blood seeped into the mountain, forming Wyrmrest Valley, where his heart still beats. Even in death he held no grudge, wishing they could have met under kinder circumstances.",
      "His remains resurfaced in Version 1.2's The Chalk Prince and the Dragon (Festering Desire was coated in his dust) and Version 2.3's Shadows Amidst Snowstorms, where his still-beating heart drove the plot.",
    ],
    relations: ["Created by Rhinedottir (Gold)", "Defeated by Barbatos and Dvalin", "Brother to Albedo"],
  },
  {
    era: "Version 4.8",
    title: "Mini Durin of Simulanka",
    body: [
      "In Simulanka — the fairytale world built by three Hexenzirkel witches — Andersdotter (M) wrote a new Durin into existence, insisting on the same name as Rhinedottir's poison dragon.",
      "This Durin was kind, but his huge form and a curse that turned everything he touched into blocks made residents fear him as an evil dragon. His longing for his mother M caused real damage, like stars falling from the sky.",
      "With the blessing of the Wanderer, the Traveler, Nilou, Navia, and Kirara, he broke free of the curse and was reborn small and harmless — the happy ending the original never had, and proof to the Wanderer that the real Durin could be saved.",
    ],
    relations: ["Created by Andersdotter", "Befriended by the Wanderer"],
  },
  {
    era: "Version 5.6 onward",
    title: "The Human Durin",
    body: [
      "After Simulanka, Albedo found the original's heart beating faster in Dragonspine — a resurrection was coming. To prevent a second disaster, he transmuted the remains into a human body.",
      "Merged with Mini Durin, the two became one being: a human boy with dragon horns and wings, now a Mondstadt resident.",
      "He is learning to live among people — befriending Klee, occasionally scolded by Acting Grand Master Jean. In The Solution of Fate, the Traveler, Albedo, and the Wanderer help him reject his original's fate. As of Version 6.2 he is a playable 5-star Pyro sword, with Story Quest Draco Rubedo Act 1: The Magic Known as Storytelling.",
    ],
    relations: ["Brother to Albedo", "Friend to Klee", "Playable since 6.2"],
  },
];

const officialVideos = [
  {
    title: "Character Trailer — Durin: A Story Born for This",
    url: "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MOkyO-PYAGY",
    note: "The official 6.2 trailer that introduced his playable design.",
  },
  {
    title: "Character Teaser — Durin: A Family Letter",
    url: "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OTnW8G2VsyM",
    note: "A letter home — his Mondstadt life with Albedo and Klee.",
  },
  {
    title: "Character Anecdote — Every Stroke of the Story",
    url: "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=aE5MofefW5c",
    note: "A later official anecdote following his story after rerun.",
  },
];

const voicelines = [
  {
    speaker: "Durin on Albedo",
    text: "Albedo has shared so many of his experiences with me regarding becoming truly human... with Albedo as my brother, I'm filled with a sense of peace and belonging.",
    source: "In-game voice-over · 'About the Family'",
  },
  {
    speaker: "Varka on Durin",
    text: "What was once one of the greatest threats to Mondstadt is now one of our most reliable allies. Fate sure is an unpredictable force.",
    source: "Official letter from the Grand Master · Version 6.2",
  },
  {
    speaker: "Nicole on Durin",
    text: "I cannot wait to see how this final, ever-evolving masterpiece of hers is going to unfold — and I will protect it at all costs.",
    source: "Official story teaser · 'What Still Lies Unwritten'",
  },
];
---

<section id="lore" class="reveal border-b border-stone-800/70 py-16 sm:py-20">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 sm:px-6">
    <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-stone-50 sm:text-4xl">
      Durin's Story: Three Forms, One Name
    </h2>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-base leading-relaxed text-stone-400">
      Durin has existed in three forms across Genshin Impact's story — knowing all three clears
      up most of the confusion around who he is.
    </p>

    <img
      src="/official/teaser-key.webp"
      alt="Official Genshin Impact key art for Durin's character teaser 'A Family Letter'"
      width="1280"
      height="720"
      loading="lazy"
      decoding="async"
      class="mt-8 w-full rounded-2xl border border-stone-800"
    />

    <ol class="relative mt-12 space-y-12 border-l border-stone-800 pl-8">
      {stages.map((s) => (
        <li class="relative">
          <span
            class="absolute -left-[2.35rem] top-1 h-3 w-3 rounded-full bg-ember-500 ring-4 ring-stone-950"
            aria-hidden="true"
          ></span>
          <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-ember-400">{s.era}</p>
          <h3 class="mt-2 text-xl font-bold tracking-tight text-stone-100">{s.title}</h3>
          <div class="mt-3 max-w-3xl space-y-3">
            {s.body.map((p) => (
              <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-stone-400">{p}</p>
            ))}
          </div>
          <div class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-2">
            {s.relations.map((r) => (
              <span class="rounded-full border border-stone-700 px-3 py-1 text-xs text-stone-400">
                {r}
              </span>
            ))}
          </div>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ol>

    <div class="mt-8 rounded-2xl border border-stone-800 bg-stone-900/40 p-6">
      <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-stone-100">In their words</h3>
      <div class="mt-4 space-y-5">
        {voicelines.map((v) => (
          <div class="border-l-2 border-ember-700/50 pl-4">
            <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-ember-400">{v.speaker}</p>
            <blockquote class="mt-1">
              <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-stone-400">{v.text}</p>
            </blockquote>
            <cite class="mt-1 block text-xs not-italic text-stone-600">— {v.source}</cite>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-8 rounded-2xl border border-stone-800 bg-stone-900/40 p-6">
      <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-stone-100">Watch the official story</h3>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-stone-400">
        Official media from HoYoverse's Genshin Impact channel — the same story told on-screen.
      </p>
      <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3">
        {officialVideos.map((v) => (
          <li>
            <a
              href={v.url}
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener"
              class="group flex items-start gap-3"
            >
              <span class="mt-0.5 flex h-9 w-9 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full border border-ember-700/50 text-ember-400 transition-colors group-hover:bg-ember-500 group-hover:text-stone-950" aria-hidden="true">
                <svg width="13" height="13" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path d="M8 5v14l11-7z" /></svg>
              </span>
              <span>
                <span class="block text-base font-medium text-stone-200 transition-colors group-hover:text-ember-300">{v.title}</span>
                <span class="block text-sm text-stone-500">{v.note}</span>
              </span>
            </a>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
